GPU ChIMES NVE test
===================

Overview
--------
NVE ensemble run of 512 carbon atoms using the Carbon-2.0 (2+3+4B,
Tersoff cutoff) ChIMES force field, executed with the CUDA GPU path.

The test verifies that GPU-computed energies and forces produce the
same macroscopic thermodynamics as the CPU reference (stored in
../test_suite-NVE/expected_output/).  A tolerance of 1e-3 is used
instead of the CPU-to-CPU value of 1e-5 to accommodate expected
non-determinism from GPU floating-point atomicAdd reductions.

Files
-----
in.lammps              LAMMPS input (identical physics to test_suite-NVE,
                        references the same data/parameter files)
run_gpu_test.sh        Interactive runner (use inside an idev GPU session)
submit_stampede3.slurm SLURM batch script for the gpu-h100 partition
compare_gpu.py         Comparison script with configurable tolerance


Prerequisites
-------------
1. The GPU-enabled LAMMPS binary must be built first:

       cd <repo>/etc/lmp
       module load intel/24.0 impi/21.11 cuda/12.4
       ./install_gpu.sh          # builds exe/lmp_mpi_chimes_gpu

   See etc/lmp/install_gpu.sh for per-machine module/hosttype details.

2. A GPU compute node (login nodes do not have GPUs).


Running on Stampede3 -- interactive session
-------------------------------------------
# Step 1: obtain an interactive GPU node (H100)
idev -p gpu-h100 -N 1 -n 1 --gpus=1 -t 00:30:00 -A <YOUR_ALLOCATION>

# Step 2: load modules (same as used for the build)
module load intel/24.0 impi/21.11 cuda/12.4 python3/3.11

# Step 3: run the test
cd <repo>/etc/lmp/tests/test_suite-GPU_NVE
./run_gpu_test.sh

Expected output (current_output/):
  out.lammps   -- LAMMPS stdout (thermo table)
  log.lammps   -- LAMMPS log file
  compare.log  -- empty if PASS, discrepancies listed if FAIL


Running on Stampede3 -- batch submission
----------------------------------------
# Edit submit_stampede3.slurm and replace <YOUR_ALLOCATION>
# with your TACC project allocation code.

sbatch submit_stampede3.slurm

Monitor with:  squeue -u $USER
Results in:    current_output/


Manual one-liner (from an interactive GPU node)
-----------------------------------------------
srun -n 1 ../../exe/lmp_mpi_chimes_gpu -i in.lammps | tee out.lammps
python3 compare_gpu.py ../test_suite-NVE/expected_output/log.lammps \
        log.lammps 1e-3


Tolerance rationale
-------------------
GPU floating-point sums are non-associative because multiple CUDA threads
atomically accumulate forces and energies using atomicAdd.  The order of
additions depends on thread scheduling and varies between runs.  For
double-precision IEEE 754 arithmetic this causes per-value differences on
the order of a few ULP (units in the last place), which propagates to
~1e-4 differences in per-step thermo quantities after 100 steps.  A
tolerance of 1e-3 provides comfortable margin while still catching genuine
physics errors.
